a_per_play":-0.4524,"pass_rate":0.569,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5278,"def_epa_per_play":-0.06999}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"MIA","distance":0.7001,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Mike McDaniel"},{"season":2023,"team":"ATL","distance":0.8033,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"CHI","distance":0.8229,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"WAS","distance":0.867,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"BAL","distance":0.8819,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Todd Monken"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"PHI","distance":0.09681,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"MIA","distance":0.2529,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vic Fangio"},{"season":2022,"team":"PHI","distance":0.2588,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Jonathan Gannon"},{"season":2022,"team":"CIN","distance":0.2643,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"},{"season":2025,"team":"BAL","distance":0.2689,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Chargers are 0-7 through week 8 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 175 to 99. The defense has done most of the work, ranking 9th in EPA allowed while the offense sits 32nd in EPA per play. Their most distinctive trait is the lowest early-down pass rate in the league.","offense":"The Chargers offense has struggled, ranking 25th or worse in all five main efficiency measures. They have been one of the most run-heavy teams in the league, passing less often than game situations would predict. Schematically, they stand out for the most backs in the backfield and the 3rd highest pre-snap motion rate in the league. Justin Herbert has run the passing game, with Tre Harris leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Chargers defense has been well above average by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the pass than the run, ranking 8th and 22nd. Tuli Tuipulotu has led the way with 3 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a blitz rate that ranks 11th lowest in the league.","special":"The Chargers have been one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 12% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers have made 86% of field goals, which is about average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the quarterback, about 24% of the money on the books. Their linebackers were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Justin Herbert has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,398 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Tre Harris and Oronde Gadsden II leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. Omarion Hampton has handled most of the work in the backfield with 55% of the carries. On defense, Tuli Tuipulotu leads the team with 3 sacks and Cam Hart has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Mike McDaniel is calling the offense and Chris O'Leary is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 Dolphins under Mike McDaniel and the 2023 Falcons. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Eagles and the 2023 Dolphins under Vic Fangio.","trends":"The offense went from 25th in EPA per play in 2025 to 32nd so far this season, a modest decline. The defense moved from 7th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 9th so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was pass rate over expected, which went from 0.64 to -9.69.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}